<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
  The button bar layout this mod ships as its default.

  Read only when the player has no layout of their own. The moment they arrange the bar in the UI options
  page their arrangement is written to UIOverhaul_ButtonBar.xml in RimWorld's config folder, and this file
  stops being consulted. Editing it changes what a new player sees, not what an existing one has.

  The root element and the entry shape match what the options page writes, so this file can be copied
  straight into the config folder and hand-edited from there if that is ever useful.

  Order here is the order on the bar. Anything not listed is appended, so a newly installed mod's tab
  lands at the end rather than disappearing. The list is still deliberately complete for the tabs that
  ship with the game and its expansions: an appended tab arrives in def-database order, which is not the
  same as the game's own button order, so naming them is what guarantees the arrangement below.

  Entries naming a tab that is not loaded are skipped and left alone, which is why the expansion tabs can
  be listed unconditionally.

  The one deliberate placement: Pawns sits directly after Architect. Vanilla's own orders are Architect 1
  and Work 10, and Pawns answers the question asked before opening Work or Schedule, which is who needs
  attention and who is doing what.
-->
<ButtonBar>

  <entry><tab>Inspect</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Architect</tab></entry>

  <!-- This mod's pawns tab. -->
  <entry><tab>Gideon_Pawns</tab></entry>

  <entry><tab>Work</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Schedule</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Assign</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Animals</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Wildlife</tab></entry>

  <!-- Also this mod's. It lists growing zones, so it belongs beside the other census tabs. -->
  <entry><tab>GZP_GrowZones</tab></entry>

  <entry><tab>Research</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Quests</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>World</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>History</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Factions</tab></entry>

  <!-- Expansion tabs. Skipped without the expansion, so listing them is free. -->
  <entry><tab>Ideos</tab></entry>
  <entry><tab>Mechs</tab></entry>

  <!-- Last, as vanilla has it: order 500 against everything else's double digits. -->
  <entry><tab>Menu</tab></entry>

</ButtonBar>
